---
description: Minimal diffs, few comments, understand the code before editing, imports at the top of the file.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Code quality

- Write clean, efficient code with minimal comments. Do not repeat what the code already shows.
- Comment only a non-obvious invariant, workaround, ordering/locking requirement, or deliberate trade-off. Do not narrate the diff or describe non-local behavior — that belongs in the PR or commit message.
- Make the smallest change that solves the problem.
- Explore and understand the codebase before editing.
- If a function or file grows a lot, split it when that is clearly better.
- Keep imports at the top of the file unless a circular, conditional, or delayed import requires otherwise.
